@flexiarg snatch/non-binding-talk-still-moves-play
@title Non-Binding Talk Still Moves Play
@audience institution designers, channel authors
@tone analytical
@style pattern
@why snatch/protect-the-unprotected-move snatch/institutions-vary-by-position-and-force

! conclusion: Open a channel before the decision even when nothing said in it can bind, and record that it was used.

  + context: Snatch or Share, variant G5 ("cheap talk"). Before the round, both
    players may write in a non-binding chat — *"sin compromisos"*. The action
    space, the payoffs and the sanctioning apparatus are identical to G1.
    Nothing said is enforceable.

  + IF:
    You want more cooperation and cannot or will not add enforcement.

  + HOWEVER:
    Promises made in an unenforceable channel change no payoff, and a player who
    reasons only from payoffs should ignore them entirely.

  + THEN:
    Open the channel anyway, place it before the decision, and record that it was
    used.

  + BECAUSE:
    A channel does not change what either party *may* do; it changes what each
    believes the other *will* do, and the choice is made against that belief.
    The intervention is on the observation, not on the action set.
    + evidence: G5 changes nothing but the channel and is retained as a distinct
      treatment, which is a claim that the channel alone is expected to matter.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    - Where a channel is proposed, separate the question "is it scored?" from
      "does it exist?" — the second is cheaper and may be sufficient.
